@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-commencement`

-- ca-tests-transition.l4
--
-- Section 5(4), section 7 (the permission limb) and the Related Provisions item, 1998, c. 30, s. 10: the commencement module.
-- Expected values written from the text before the module was run.
-- The dates in the Related Provisions cases are invented for the test: the text gives no day on which section 10 of the 1998 Act came into force.

GIVEN assent IS A DATE
      says IS A `What an enactment says about when it comes into force`
GIVETH A `Commencement facts of an Act`
`a transition-test Act assented to on` assent `that` says MEANS
    `Commencement facts of an Act`
        WITH `the day the Act was assented to` IS assent
             `what the provision says about when it comes into force` IS says

§ `Section 5(4): the remaining provisions of an Act`

-- The Act gives some provisions another day, and the provision asked about is not one of them: section 5(4) deems it in force on the date of assent.
#ASSERT `section 5(4) deems a provision of an Act to have come into force on the date of assent, given that` TRUE `and` TRUE
-- The provision asked about is one of the provisions given another day: section 5(4) does not deem it; it has its own day.
#ASSERT NOT (`section 5(4) deems a provision of an Act to have come into force on the date of assent, given that` TRUE `and` FALSE)
-- No provision of the Act names a day other than the date of assent: the subsection's condition is not met, so it deems nothing (#52).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 5(4) deems a provision of an Act to have come into force on the date of assent, given that` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 5(4) deems a provision of an Act to have come into force on the date of assent, given that` FALSE `and` FALSE)
-- The date is the date of assent.
#ASSERT `the date on which the remaining provisions of an Act are deemed to have come into force, the Act being assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
-- It is the same date as subsection 5(2) gives for an Act that provides none, and as the moment s 6(2)(a) fixes (the expiration of the day before).
#ASSERT `the date on which the remaining provisions of an Act are deemed to have come into force, the Act being assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS `the date of commencement of an Act that provides none, assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`a transition-test Act assented to on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `that` `it names no day`) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 9))

§ `Section 7: a power exercised before commencement`

-- A power to make regulations, in an enactment not yet in force that contains the provisions conferring it, exercised for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement: it may be exercised before commencement (#71).
#ASSERT `a power of the kind` `a power to make regulations` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` TRUE `and` TRUE `and` TRUE
-- "Or do any other thing": a power to do a thing other than make a regulation is covered alike (#76).
#ASSERT `a power of the kind` `a power to do any other thing` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` TRUE `and` TRUE `and` TRUE
-- The permission is "for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement"; an exercise for another purpose is not within it, and the Act does not say whether it is otherwise allowed (#75).
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power of the kind` `a power to make regulations` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` TRUE `and` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power of the kind` `a power to do any other thing` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` TRUE `and` TRUE `and` FALSE)
-- The section speaks of "an enactment [that] is not in force"; it says nothing of an enactment already in force.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power of the kind` `a power to make regulations` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` FALSE `and` TRUE `and` TRUE)
-- The section speaks of an enactment that "contains provisions conferring power"; it says nothing of a power the enactment does not confer.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power of the kind` `a power to make regulations` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` TRUE `and` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a power of the kind` `a power to do any other thing` `may be exercised before the commencement of the enactment where` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE)
-- The second limb, already in the time module: what is so made or done has no effect before commencement unless necessary to make the enactment effective.
#ASSERT NOT (`a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `where the enactment is first in force on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `where the enactment is first in force on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `and` TRUE

§ `Related Provisions, 1998, c. 30, s. 10: a proceeding commenced before that section came into force`

-- Commenced well before the day the section is first in force, and a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 applies: taken up and continued under the amended provision.
#ASSERT `a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` (YMD 2000 3 1) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE
-- Commenced on the day before the section is first in force: still before the coming into force.
#ASSERT `a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` (YMD 2000 5 31) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE
-- Commenced on the day the section is first in force: section 6(1) puts the coming into force at the first moment of that day, so this is not before it, and the text says nothing of it.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE)
-- Commenced after: the text says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` (YMD 2000 6 2) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` (YMD 2001 1 1) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE)
-- Commenced before, but no provision amended by sections 12 to 16 applies to it: there is no amended provision to take it up under, and the text says nothing.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision, being commenced on` (YMD 2000 3 1) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` FALSE)
-- "Without any further formality": no further formality is needed, for the case the section addresses.
#ASSERT NOT (`a further formality is needed to take up and continue under the amended provision a proceeding commenced on` (YMD 2000 3 1) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE)
-- Outside that case the text does not say whether a formality is needed.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a further formality is needed to take up and continue under the amended provision a proceeding commenced on` (YMD 2000 6 2) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a further formality is needed to take up and continue under the amended provision a proceeding commenced on` (YMD 2000 3 1) `where the section is first in force on` (YMD 2000 6 1) `and` FALSE)
